From 5031fb96fa12706f75389a6a753890853f61d0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phillippe Pelzer <phil.pelzer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:13:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add HLS playlist generation functions

This commit introduces a new header file `hlsplaylist.h` and its corresponding implementation file `hlsplaylist.c` for generating Apple HTTP Live Streaming (HLS) playlists. The new functions include:

- `ff_hls_write_playlist_version`: Writes the playlist version.
- `ff_hls_write_audio_rendition`: Writes audio rendition information.
- `ff_hls_write_subtitle_rendition`: Writes subtitle rendition information.
- `ff_hls_write_stream_info`: Writes stream information including bandwidth and resolution.
- `ff_hls_write_playlist_header`: Writes the header for the HLS playlist.
- `ff_hls_write_init_file`: Writes initialization file information.
- `ff_hls_write_file_entry`: Writes individual file entries in the playlist.
- `ff_hls_write_end_list`: Marks the end of the playlist.

These functions facilitate the creation of HLS playlists, adhering to the specifications outlined in RFC 8216.

#/**************************************/#
#/*  NoMercy Entertainment — HLS       */#
#/*  master playlist spec compliance   */#
#/**************************************/#

# Replace the upstream HLS muxer sources with patched versions that complete
# the master playlist for Apple HLS spec compliance:
#   - FRAME-RATE and VIDEO-RANGE (SDR/PQ/HLG) on #EXT-X-STREAM-INF
#   - aname: var_stream_map key for a custom audio rendition NAME
#   - auto-set the hvc1 tag on HEVC streams instead of silently
#     dropping the CODECS attribute
#   - HEVC codec string from hvcC extradata (stream copies from MP4/MOV)
#   - loud warning when a CODECS attribute cannot be built
# See: https://github.com/NoMercy-Entertainment/nomercy-ffmpeg/issues/12

---
